  "instruction": "Read context files, work through pending tasks, mark complete as you go.\nPause if you hit blockers or need clarification.",
  "context": "This is a small C99/X11 dmenu fork with POSIX shell launchers, not a service.\nIts public interface is CLI flags, keyboard interaction, stdin/stdout, and exit status.\nFuzzy matching is the default; -F retains token matching and -i affects case handling.\nConfiguration is compiled in; existing local config.h files are not refreshed from config.def.h.\n",
  "operationGuidance": [
    "Inspect live source before using patches/; stored patch files are not an application manifest.",
    "Preserve local config.h customizations; make clean does not regenerate that file.",
